# R-132: regression found and fixed inside the batch (recorded as it happened)
# AFTER v1 (named pools + web queue cap 8, AGOS_POOL_WEB=4):
#   - 169/170: reachability fixed (p50 19.98 s -> 0.08 s at 50), but the web pool queue reached 41 and,
#     with no wait bound in educator's web fallback, llm_first (educator) p95 50.19 s -> 119.95 s at 50.
#   - pytest: tests/test_specialist_runtime.py::test_r105_specialists_impl_still_builds_1000
#     AssertionError: expected 1000/1000, got 996/1000
#   - /tmp/r132_which.py (1000 concurrent tasks, live web):
#       39 ('researcher', 'search: web pool busy: 8 call(s) already waiting for 4 thread(s) (cap AGOS_POOL_WEB_QUEUE=8)')
#     -> the cap rejected researcher searches although researcher already bounds its wait by its own budget.
# FIX (final): queue caps are opt-in (default 0 for every pool); educator web fallback and communicator
#   translation bound their total wait with asyncio.wait_for(AGOS_WEB_WAIT_S=20); a call cancelled while
#   queued never runs (tests/test_r132_pools.py::test_wait_cancelled_while_queued_never_runs).
# After the fix: pytest 473 passed (test_r105... passes again).
# Live-web note: /tmp/r132_which.py then gave 950/1000 on BOTH old (5e93d8a) and new code, all 50
#   failures 'researcher: search: overall budget exceeded (transient ...)' — DuckDuckGo refusing a burst
#   of 50 from this host after the load runs; same on both, so not caused by R-132.

